From 4439d623e8c4d7ad70debd6153911a4fe053743c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] backends/monitor: Keep color settings when copying
 layouts

Configuration copies made for orientation changes and for amending a
layout dropped the color mode, RGB range and target override. Keep
them. When a layout is synthesized, recover each monitor's target
override by monitor identity from the existing configuration history;
an explicit replacement over D-Bus stays separate. Mirrored monitors
each take their own color mode from the history.

Add monitor storage tests for copies, history lookup, that a VERIFY
request does not change anything, and that applying an override alone
reapplies the configuration.

Link: TBD-MR
